<item>
            <title>[LU-20556] LOD: skip per-stripe OST availability walk when all OSTs are healthy</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20556</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Several LOD paths decide &#8220;is this stripe / mirror usable?&#8221; by walking components and calling&#160;&lt;tt&gt;lod_check_ost_avail()&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;for each OST object (FLD lookup +&#160;&lt;tt&gt;ltd_active&lt;/tt&gt;):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lod_primary_pick()&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;&#8212; FLR write-primary selection (hot path on write intent)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lod_layout_has_unavailable_stripe()&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;&#8212; non-FLR trunc(0) unavailable check (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20211&quot; title=&quot;FLR-ECRO: allow &apos;truncate(file, 0)&apos; and &apos;open(file, O_TRUNC)&apos; on degraded EC file&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20211&quot;&gt;LU-20211&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;In a healthy cluster these walks almost always find every OST active, so most of the work is wasted&#8212;especially on&#160;&lt;tt&gt;lod_primary_pick()&lt;/tt&gt;, which can run far more often than trunc(0).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Andreas suggested maintaining a single top-level bit (or bitmask) for &#8220;any OST currently unavailable&#8221;, so the common all-healthy case can skip the per-object walk. A race between updating that summary and a full check is acceptable and no worse than today (an OST can go offline immediately after a successful check).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Proposal&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposal&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Track a summary of OST activity on the LOD OST target table. Prefer reusing existing&#160;&lt;tt&gt;ld_active_tgt_count&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;(updated when&#160;&lt;tt&gt;ltd_active&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;flips in qos/statfs and related paths); add an explicit bit/bitmask only if needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fast path for both callers:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;All OSTs healthy (&lt;tt&gt;ld_active_tgt_count == ld_tgt_count&lt;/tt&gt;, or summary bit clear) &#8594; skip per-stripe&#160;&lt;tt&gt;lod_check_ost_avail()&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;walks.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Otherwise &#8594; keep the existing per-stripe checks for that object/mirror.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Update the summary in the same places that already change&#160;&lt;tt&gt;ltd_active&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;(mainly LOD qos/statfs under&#160;&lt;tt&gt;lod_lock&lt;/tt&gt;, plus target add / process_config). Consumers are&#160;&lt;tt&gt;lod_primary_pick&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;and unavailable-layout checks.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
